=== Post-1709: Autonomous Republic ===

Following the [[Burawi Imperial Split]] of 1709, Lacashe was reconstituted as an '''autonomous parliamentary republic'''. The '''Parliament of Lacashe''' was established as the legislative body, with membership restricted to men who owned land (initially 25 acres or more). The parliament legislated on internal affairs: taxation, property law, criminal justice, and public works.

The '''Governor of Lacashe''' served as the chief executive and the liaison with the metropolitan government. The Governor was selected by the Parliament of Lacashe from among the planter elite and confirmed by the crown. The Governor administered the civil service, commanded the provincial militia, and corresponded with Samara on matters of provincial concern. Foreign affairs — including trade policy, treaties, and military commitments — remained under Burawi control; the Governor had no authority to conduct diplomacy or negotiate with foreign powers.

